what-the-commit-field-means: the commit whose CONTENT this record was computed from,
  which is the commit holding the region files it read.  This record is necessarily
  written afterwards and therefore lands in a SUCCESSOR commit; a record cannot
  contain the hash of the commit that contains it.  The clean-worktree assertion
  above is what makes the field meaningful rather than decorative: it establishes
  that the regions this record describes were committed, unmodified, at that
  revision.  Stating a hash without that assertion is what made an earlier
  evidence set unusable.
source: the ten startup regions in baseline/startup/
