gate: AAP 0.9.4 — deployment reaches ready state with no migration-attributable
  ERROR entry, and the process engine's loaded definition total observed

GATE-OUTCOME: PASS
  This outcome is shared by both sides, because its central condition is a
  statement about the PAIR: an error shape is attributable to the migration only
  if it is absent before it and present after.  A per-side verdict could not
  express that and would invite the two sides to disagree.

